  1	# Session File Format
  2	
  3	Sessions are stored as JSONL (JSON Lines) files. Each line is a JSON object with a `type` field. Session entries form a tree structure via `id`/`parentId` fields, enabling in-place branching without creating new files.
  4	
  5	## File Location
  6	
  7	```
  8	~/.pi/agent/sessions/--<path>--/<timestamp>_<uuid>.jsonl
  9	```
 10	
 11	Where `<path>` is the working directory with `/` replaced by `-`.
 12	
 13	## Deleting Sessions
 14	
 15	Sessions can be removed by deleting their `.jsonl` files under `~/.pi/agent/sessions/`.
 16	
 17	Pi also supports deleting sessions interactively from `/resume` (select a session and press `Ctrl+D`, then confirm). When available, pi uses the `trash` CLI to avoid permanent deletion.
 18	
 19	## Session Version
 20	
 21	Sessions have a version field in the header:
 22	
 23	- **Version 1**: Linear entry sequence (legacy, auto-migrated on load)
 24	- **Version 2**: Tree structure with `id`/`parentId` linking
 25	- **Version 3**: Renamed `hookMessage` role to `custom` (extensions unification)
 26	
 27	Existing sessions are automatically migrated to the current version (v3) when loaded.
 28	
 29	## Source Files
 30	
 31	Source on GitHub ([pi-mono](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono)):
 32	- [`packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts`](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/src/core/session-manager.ts) - Session entry types and SessionManager
 33	- [`packages/coding-agent/src/core/messages.ts`](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/src/core/messages.ts) - Extended message types (BashExecutionMessage, CustomMessage, etc.)
 34	- [`packages/ai/src/types.ts`](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts) - Base message types (UserMessage, AssistantMessage, ToolResultMessage)
 35	- [`packages/agent/src/types.ts`](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/agent/src/types.ts) - AgentMessage union type
 36	
 37	For TypeScript definitions in your project, inspect `node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist/` and `node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-ai/dist/`.
 38	
 39	## Message Types
 40	
 41	Session entries contain `AgentMessage` objects. Understanding these types is essential for parsing sessions and writing extensions.
 42	
 43	### Content Blocks
 44	
 45	Messages contain arrays of typed content blocks:
 46	
 47	```typescript
 48	interface TextContent {
 49	  type: "text";
 50	  text: string;
 51	}
 52	
 53	interface ImageContent {
 54	  type: "image";
 55	  data: string;      // base64 encoded
 56	  mimeType: string;  // e.g., "image/jpeg", "image/png"
 57	}
 58	
 59	interface ThinkingContent {
 60	  type: "thinking";
 61	  thinking: string;
 62	}
 63	
 64	interface ToolCall {
 65	  type: "toolCall";
 66	  id: string;
 67	  name: string;
 68	  arguments: Record<string, any>;
 69	}
 70	```
 71	
 72	### Base Message Types (from pi-ai)
 73	
 74	```typescript
 75	interface UserMessage {
 76	  role: "user";
 77	  content: string | (TextContent | ImageContent)[];
 78	  timestamp: number;  // Unix ms
 79	}
 80	
 81	interface AssistantMessage {
 82	  role: "assistant";
 83	  content: (TextContent | ThinkingContent | ToolCall)[];
 84	  api: string;
 85	  provider: string;
 86	  model: string;
 87	  usage: Usage;
 88	  stopReason: "stop" | "length" | "toolUse" | "error" | "aborted";
 89	  errorMessage?: string;
 90	  timestamp: number;
 91	}
 92	
 93	interface ToolResultMessage {
 94	  role: "toolResult";
 95	  toolCallId: string;
 96	  toolName: string;
 97	  content: (TextContent | ImageContent)[];
 98	  details?: any;      // Tool-specific metadata
 99	  usage?: Usage;      // Nested LLM work performed by the tool
100	  isError: boolean;
101	  timestamp: number;
102	}
103	
104	interface Usage {
105	  input: number;
106	  output: number;
107	  cacheRead: number;
108	  cacheWrite: number;
109	  totalTokens: number;
110	  cost: {
111	    input: number;
112	    output: number;
113	    cacheRead: number;
114	    cacheWrite: number;
115	    total: number;
116	  };
117	}
118	```
119	
120	### Extended Message Types (from pi-coding-agent)
121	
122	```typescript
123	interface BashExecutionMessage {
124	  role: "bashExecution";
125	  command: string;
126	  output: string;
127	  exitCode: number | undefined;
128	  cancelled: boolean;
129	  truncated: boolean;
130	  fullOutputPath?: string;
131	  excludeFromContext?: boolean;  // true for !! prefix commands
132	  timestamp: number;
133	}
134	
135	interface CustomMessage {
136	  role: "custom";
137	  customType: string;            // Extension identifier
138	  content: string | (TextContent | ImageContent)[];
139	  display: boolean;              // Show in TUI
140	  details?: any;                 // Extension-specific metadata
141	  timestamp: number;
142	}
143	
144	interface BranchSummaryMessage {
145	  role: "branchSummary";
146	  summary: string;
147	  fromId: string;                // Entry we branched from
148	  timestamp: number;
149	}
150	
151	interface CompactionSummaryMessage {
152	  role: "compactionSummary";
153	  summary: string;
154	  tokensBefore: number;
155	  timestamp: number;
156	}
157	```
158	
159	### AgentMessage Union
160	
161	```typescript
162	type AgentMessage =
163	  | UserMessage
164	  | AssistantMessage
165	  | ToolResultMessage
166	  | BashExecutionMessage
167	  | CustomMessage
168	  | BranchSummaryMessage
169	  | CompactionSummaryMessage;
170	```
171	
172	## Entry Base
173	
174	All entries (except `SessionHeader`) extend `SessionEntryBase`:
175	
176	```typescript
177	interface SessionEntryBase {
178	  type: string;
179	  id: string;           // 8-char hex ID
180	  parentId: string | null;  // Parent entry ID (null for first entry)
181	  timestamp: string;    // ISO timestamp
182	}
183	```
184	
185	## Entry Types
186	
187	### SessionHeader
188	
189	First line of the file. Metadata only, not part of the tree (no `id`/`parentId`).
190	
191	```json
192	{"type":"session","version":3,"id":"uuid","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","cwd":"/path/to/project"}
193	```
194	
195	For sessions with a parent (created via `/fork`, `/clone`, or `newSession({ parentSession })`):
196	
197	```json
198	{"type":"session","version":3,"id":"uuid","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:00:00.000Z","cwd":"/path/to/project","parentSession":"/path/to/original/session.jsonl"}
199	```
200	
201	### SessionMessageEntry
202	
203	A message in the conversation. The `message` field contains an `AgentMessage`.
204	
205	```json
206	{"type":"message","id":"a1b2c3d4","parentId":"prev1234","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:00:01.000Z","message":{"role":"user","content":"Hello"}}
207	{"type":"message","id":"b2c3d4e5","parentId":"a1b2c3d4","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:00:02.000Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Hi!"}],"provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","usage":{...},"stopReason":"stop"}}
208	{"type":"message","id":"c3d4e5f6","parentId":"b2c3d4e5","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:00:03.000Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_123","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"output"}],"isError":false}}
209	```
210	
211	### ModelChangeEntry
212	
213	Emitted when the user switches models mid-session.
214	
215	```json
216	{"type":"model_change","id":"d4e5f6g7","parentId":"c3d4e5f6","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:05:00.000Z","provider":"openai","modelId":"gpt-4o"}
217	```
218	
219	### ThinkingLevelChangeEntry
220	
221	Emitted when the user changes the thinking/reasoning level.
222	
223	```json
224	{"type":"thinking_level_change","id":"e5f6g7h8","parentId":"d4e5f6g7","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:06:00.000Z","thinkingLevel":"high"}
225	```
226	
227	### CompactionEntry
228	
229	Created when context is compacted. Stores a summary of earlier messages.
230	
231	```json
232	{"type":"compaction","id":"f6g7h8i9","parentId":"e5f6g7h8","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:10:00.000Z","summary":"User discussed X, Y, Z...","firstKeptEntryId":"c3d4e5f6","tokensBefore":50000}
233	```
234	
235	Newer harness-generated compactions embed the retained post-compaction context directly on the entry, instead of `firstKeptEntryId`:
236	
237	```json
238	{"type":"compaction","id":"f6g7h8i9","parentId":"e5f6g7h8","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:10:00.000Z","summary":"User discussed X, Y, Z...","tokensBefore":50000,"retainedTail":[{"role":"user","content":"latest request"},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"latest reply"}],"provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","usage":{...},"stopReason":"stop"}]}
239	```
240	
241	Optional fields:
242	- `usage`: LLM usage from generating the summary; included in session token and cost totals
243	- `retainedTail`: Materialized `AgentMessage[]` kept after compaction. This is optional only for backward compatibility with older sessions. Newer harness-generated compactions include it so we can rebuild context from this checkpoint without walking older entries before the compaction entry.
244	- `details`: Implementation-specific data (e.g., `{ readFiles: string[], modifiedFiles: string[] }` for default, or custom data for extensions)
245	- `fromHook`: `true` if generated by an extension, `false`/`undefined` if pi-generated (legacy field name)
246	- `firstKeptEntryId`: for compatibility with old entry format.
247	
248	### BranchSummaryEntry
249	
250	Created when switching branches via `/tree` with an LLM generated summary of the left branch up to the common ancestor. Captures context from the abandoned path.
251	
252	```json
253	{"type":"branch_summary","id":"g7h8i9j0","parentId":"a1b2c3d4","timestamp":"2024-12-03T14:15:00.000Z","fromId":"f6g7h8i9","summary":"Branch explored approach A..."}
254	```
255	
256	Optional fields:
257	- `usage`: LLM usage from generating the summary; included in session token and cost totals
258	- `details`: File tracking data (`{ readFiles: string[], modifiedFiles: string[] }`) for default, or custom data for extensions
259	- `fromHook`: `true` if generated by an extension, `false`/`undefined` if pi-generated (legacy field name)
